# Example workflow: scheduled PR & issue review of a TARGET repo, draft-only.
#
# Host this in YOUR OWN fork (or any repo you control) — not in the upstream
# project (e.g. apache/ossie). You don't have merge rights there, and adding
# an automated/bot workflow to an Apache project's own CI needs PMC review.
#
# IMPORTANT: `pull_request:` / `issues:` triggers fire only for events on the
# repo that HOSTS this workflow (your fork), not on TARGET_REPO below. That's
# why this uses `schedule` / `workflow_dispatch` plus an explicit TARGET_REPO
# value, and has the job query that repo's API directly — the API calls work
# the same regardless of which repo the runner lives in.
#
# This is NOT wired up to run — it's a reference. Before using it:
#   1. Install Devin CLI in the runner (see devin.ai docs for the install step;
#      I have not confirmed an officially supported non-interactive/CI auth
#      flow exists today — check with Devin support before relying on this).
#   2. Set TARGET_REPO below to the project you want reviewed (e.g. apache/ossie).
#   3. Decide what "new" means for your sweep (e.g. PRs/issues updated since the
#      last run) — the placeholder command below reviews one fixed URL; a real
#      version would list recent items via the GitHub search API first.
#
# Key safety property: `permissions` below grants read-only access to THIS repo
# only. The job never authenticates as a user with write access to TARGET_REPO,
# so it cannot post there even if asked to — draft-only is enforced by the
# environment, not just by the prompt.

name: Apache review (draft only)

env:
  TARGET_REPO: apache/ossie   # the project being reviewed, not the repo hosting this workflow

on:
  schedule:
    - cron: "0 13 * * *"   # once a day; adjust as needed
  workflow_dispatch: {}     # lets you trigger it manually from the Actions tab

permissions:
  contents: read
  # No "write" scopes, and no token for TARGET_REPO: this job can only read
  # TARGET_REPO's public API, it cannot post comments or create issues there.

jobs:
  review:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Install Devin CLI
        run: |
          # Replace with the actual install command for your Devin CLI distribution.
          echo "install devin-cli here"

      - name: Run apache-review skill (draft only)
        id: review
        run: |
          devin -p --respect-workspace-trust false \
            "Use the apache-review skill, unattended/draft-only mode, on repo: $TARGET_REPO. \
             List open PRs/issues updated in the last day via the public GitHub API and review \
             each. Write the draft to review-draft.md." \
            | tee review-output.txt

      - name: Upload draft as an artifact
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: apache-review-draft
          path: |
            review-draft.md
            review-output.txt

      - name: Add to job summary
        run: |
          echo "## Apache review draft (not posted)" >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
          cat review-output.txt >> "$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY"
